---
// New Explore-only story: "You tapped. Approved. Who said yes?" — Card 4 of
// the four homepage preview cards. Scene 1 only, on exactly the construction
// /explore/looks-real-is-it, /explore/ai-answered-you,
// /explore/did-your-face-leave-the-phone and /explore/where-is-the-5g all
// use: one grid, copy and the interaction on the left, the visual stage on
// the right; the left title stays the anchor for the whole story once later
// scenes exist, the same way none of the other stories' opening headings
// change once their own story has started.
//
// The supplied Card4 render is the ordinary moment itself — a phone held to
// a terminal in a café, APPROVED already on screen — with nothing drawn over
// it: no payment diagram, no arrows, no bank or network branding, no
// transaction animation, no caption, no explanatory overlay. That
// ordinariness is the whole point of this opening: it happened, it took a
// second, and the question of who actually decided is what the beats past
// the CTA exist to work through.
//
// The CTA is "Who said yes?" rather than a generic "How?" on purpose. The
// homepage card has already planted that exact curiosity, and this story is
// about discovering that APPROVED is the outcome of a decision made
// somewhere in a payment system — not simply an explanation of how tapping
// works.
//
// SCENE 2 DOES NOT EXIST YET. When it is built, note that the answer to
// "who said yes?" is NOT simply "your bank". A contactless payment can
// involve the merchant, an acquirer/processor, a payment network, wallet and
// device mechanisms, and the card issuer — and authorisation can take
// different paths, including ones where the terminal or the card applies
// issuer-set rules without a live round trip. That needs the same factual
// discipline Card 3 used: reveal it carefully, scope every claim, and do not
// turn the story into a payments-architecture lesson.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { storyPageMeta } from '../../data/storyMeta';

// Title, description and share card all come from this story's entry in
// src/data/stories.ts, so there is one place each is written down. Canonical
// is left to BaseLayout's own default, which is already this page's address.
const meta = (await storyPageMeta('who-said-yes', Astro.site))!;
---

<BaseLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} image={meta.image} schema={meta.schema}>
  <div class="tap" data-tap data-stage="1">
    <!-- Same reasoning as the other openings: copy and the visual share one
         grid rather than a header sitting above a separate stage, so on wide
         screens they sit side by side and both the heading and the CTA are
         readable before the visitor scrolls past the image; below the
         stacking point they fall back to the same top-to-bottom order, copy
         first.

         Carries the same small eyebrow the other Explore openings use —
         reused as-is (small saffron dot, cobalt uppercase) rather than
         inventing a new treatment. -->
    <div class="tap__stage shell">
      <div class="tap__copy">
        <p class="tap__eyebrow"><span></span>You tapped</p>

        <h1 class="tap__opening">You tapped. Approved.</h1>

        <p class="tap__noticed">In seconds.</p>

        <!-- The one thing that starts the story. Real and focusable now, the
             same way every other story's opening control is, even though
             nothing past it exists yet. -->
        <button type="button" class="tap__show" data-show>
          Who said yes? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <!-- ====================================================
           THE VISUALS — Scene 1's photo. Later beats will take the column
           over entirely rather than sitting beside or behind it, the same
           on/off handoff every other Explore story uses; the rule that hides
           this scene is declared below so that beat doesn't need to touch it
           when it exists. -->
      <div class="tap__visuals">
        <!-- THE SCENE — the supplied Card4 render, used as-is and locked.

             A plain photograph of an ordinary purchase rather than a composed
             technical illustration, so its box is simply sized to its own
             ratio (1536 x 1024, 3:2) with no overlay, effect, label, arrow or
             transaction graphic drawn over it — and stays exactly that way
             for as long as it's on screen. -->
        <div class="tap__scene">
          <img
            class="tap__art"
            src="/images/Card4.webp"
            alt="A hand holding a phone to a card terminal on a café counter, the terminal already showing APPROVED."
            width="1536"
            height="1024"
            fetchpriority="high"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>

        <!-- ====================================================
             SCENE 2 — the tap happened here; the decision didn't.

             Exactly one new idea, and the visual carries it before any copy
             is read: everything the reader actually saw is grouped together
             under "You" on the left, then there is real empty space, then a
             question mark. The gap IS the point — it is the part of the
             moment that was never visible.

             Nothing beyond the terminal is named, drawn or hinted at. No
             bank, issuer, acquirer, network, wallet, processor or merchant
             bank; no server, cloud, map, shield, lock, logo or money. The
             only thing that crosses the gap is a small unlabelled mark
             standing for the request, and it never arrives anywhere — it
             fades before the question mark, because what it reaches is
             precisely what this beat refuses to answer. -->
        <div class="tap__moment">
          <p class="tap__travelled">
            That “Approved” travelled farther than your hand did.
          </p>

          <div class="tap__diagram" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="tap__here">
              <span class="tap__here-label">You</span>
              <span class="tap__here-art">
                <span class="tap__phone"><span class="tap__phone-speaker"></span></span>
                <span class="tap__to">→</span>
                <span class="tap__terminal">
                  <span class="tap__terminal-screen"></span>
                  <span class="tap__terminal-keys"></span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </span>

            <!-- The deliberate gap. -->
            <span class="tap__gap">
              <span class="tap__request"></span>
            </span>

            <span class="tap__unknown">?</span>
          </div>
          <p class="tap__sr-only">
            The phone and the terminal on one side, then a gap, then a question
            mark — with a small request leaving the terminal and heading into the
            gap.
          </p>

          <p class="tap__reveal-kicker">The terminal wasn't the whole decision.</p>
          <p class="tap__reveal-text">
            It sent a payment request into a system you couldn't see.
          </p>

          <!-- The way onward. -->
          <button type="button" class="tap__turn" data-went>
            Where did it go? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </button>

          <!-- ====================================================
               SCENE 3 — the request finds its way.

               Evolves Scene 2 rather than replacing it: the same "You"
               group, the same phone and terminal outlines, and the gap
               Scene 2 left empty now has something in it. The question
               mark survives and simply moves further right, because who
               decides is still not answered here.

               The payment path is drawn as one neutral region holding a
               few unnamed marks — the marks are there because the copy
               says several systems can be involved, and showing one box
               would quietly claim it is a single hop. No logo, no brand,
               no named party, no map, no server, no cloud. Nothing inside
               it is labelled or distinguishable, because naming any of it
               is exactly what this beat is not ready to do. -->
          <div class="tap__path">
            <p class="tap__found">
              First, the request had to find its way through the payment system.
            </p>

            <div class="tap__chain" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="tap__step" data-step="1">
                <span class="tap__step-label">You</span>
                <span class="tap__step-art">
                  <span class="tap__phone"><span class="tap__phone-speaker"></span></span>
                  <span class="tap__to">→</span>
                  <span class="tap__terminal">
                    <span class="tap__terminal-screen"></span>
                    <span class="tap__terminal-keys"></span>
                  </span>
                </span>
              </span>

              <span class="tap__link" data-step="2">→</span>

              <!-- Deliberately unlabelled. The dotted container stands for the
                   systems the request may travel through, and naming them here
                   would pre-empt the next beat — which is the one that reveals
                   who actually decides. The ambiguity is the point. -->
              <span class="tap__step" data-step="3">
                <span class="tap__step-art">
                  <span class="tap__route">
                    <span class="tap__route-mark"></span>
                    <span class="tap__route-mark"></span>
                    <span class="tap__route-mark"></span>
                  </span>
                </span>
              </span>

              <span class="tap__link" data-step="4">→</span>

              <span class="tap__step tap__step--end" data-step="5">
                <span class="tap__step-art">
                  <span class="tap__unknown tap__unknown--chain">?</span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </div>
            <p class="tap__sr-only">
              The phone and terminal, then a neutral stretch of the payment system
              holding a few unnamed parts, then a question mark.
            </p>

            <p class="tap__reveal-kicker">
              Some parts carry the request. Another party may decide whether to
              approve it.
            </p>
            <p class="tap__reveal-text">
              The message can pass through several systems before an answer comes
              back.
            </p>

            <!-- The way onward. -->
            <button type="button" class="tap__turn" data-decides>
              So who decides? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </button>

            <!-- ====================================================
                 SCENE 4 — the question mark resolves.

                 This beat answers rather than deferring: the "?" Scene 3
                 left standing becomes a named party in the same position
                 on the same chain, so the reveal is a substitution the
                 reader can follow, not a new diagram.

                 Scene 3 grouped the phone and terminal together under
                 "You". Here they separate, because that is the actual
                 distinction this beat turns on: the thing you tapped
                 belongs to the shop, and the decision belongs somewhere
                 else entirely. The dotted stretch between them stays
                 unlabelled, exactly as Scene 3 locked it.

                 "Usually" is doing real work in the headline and must not
                 be edited out: the deciding party is the card issuer,
                 which is often but not always a bank, and not every
                 payment arrangement authorises the same way — some
                 approvals can be made against issuer-set rules without a
                 live round trip. The supporting line carries that caveat
                 so the accessible word "bank" can stay in the headline
                 without becoming a false claim. -->
            <div class="tap__issuer">
              <p class="tap__usually">Usually, your bank decides.</p>

              <div class="tap__chain" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="tap__step" data-i="1">
                  <span class="tap__step-label">You</span>
                  <span class="tap__step-art">
                    <span class="tap__phone"><span class="tap__phone-speaker"></span></span>
                  </span>
                </span>

                <span class="tap__link" data-i="2">→</span>

                <span class="tap__step" data-i="3">
                  <span class="tap__step-label">Merchant</span>
                  <span class="tap__step-art">
                    <span class="tap__terminal">
                      <span class="tap__terminal-screen"></span>
                      <span class="tap__terminal-keys"></span>
                    </span>
                  </span>
                </span>

                <span class="tap__link" data-i="4">→</span>

                <!-- Still unlabelled, as locked in Scene 3. -->
                <span class="tap__step" data-i="5">
                  <span class="tap__step-art">
                    <span class="tap__route">
                      <span class="tap__route-mark"></span>
                      <span class="tap__route-mark"></span>
                      <span class="tap__route-mark"></span>
                    </span>
                  </span>
                </span>

                <span class="tap__link" data-i="6">→</span>

                <!-- Where the "?" stood. -->
                <span class="tap__step" data-i="7">
                  <span class="tap__step-label tap__step-label--answer">Your bank</span>
                  <span class="tap__step-art">
                    <span class="tap__bank"><span class="tap__bank-mark"></span></span>
                  </span>
                </span>
              </div>
              <p class="tap__sr-only">
                The same chain as before, with the question mark at the end now
                replaced by your bank.
              </p>

              <!-- Familiar idea first, technical name second. The term
                   "issuer" is deliberately not used until the sentence
                   above has already described the thing it names; naming
                   first and explaining after would make the reader work
                   backwards. The "though not always" is load-bearing —
                   the issuer is often but not always a bank. -->
              <p class="tap__reveal-kicker">
                The bank behind your card checks the request and decides whether to
                approve it.
              </p>
              <p class="tap__reveal-text">
                <span class="tap__line">In payment systems, this is called the issuer.</span>
                <span class="tap__line">It is usually a bank, though not always.</span>
              </p>

              <!-- The way onward. -->
              <button type="button" class="tap__turn" data-checks>
                What does it check? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              </button>

              <!-- ====================================================
                   SCENE 5 — more than one thing.

                   The story stops drawing the payment path here. Nothing in
                   this beat revisits who the issuer is, how the request got
                   there, or what the terminal did — it is only about what
                   goes into the decision.

                   Set as a 2x2 grid on purpose. A row with arrows would say
                   "first this, then that", which would be wrong: these are
                   considerations weighed together, not stages. So there are
                   no connectors, no numbers, no ordering cues, and all four
                   carry identical treatment so none reads as the first or
                   the decisive one. They arrive on a very tight stagger so
                   the group settles at once rather than counting itself out.

                   Deliberately absent: any pass/fail mark, tick, cross,
                   meter, score, percentage or panel. Showing a result per
                   signal would turn four examples into a verdict, and would
                   also imply all four always run and always run this way.
                   The supporting line carries that caveat instead.

                   These are illustrative examples, not an authorisation
                   algorithm. Nothing here names CVV/CVC, PIN, 3-D Secure,
                   tokenisation, cryptograms, fraud-model internals, merchant
                   category codes, network rules, authorisation codes, any
                   card network or any bank — all of which would trade the
                   concept for machinery. -->
              <div class="tap__signals">
                <p class="tap__notone">It doesn't check just one thing.</p>

                <ul class="tap__grid">
                  <li class="tap__signal" data-s="1">
                    <span class="tap__signal-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <p class="tap__signal-label">Your account</p>
                    <p class="tap__signal-q">Enough funds or credit?</p>
                  </li>

                  <li class="tap__signal" data-s="2">
                    <span class="tap__signal-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <p class="tap__signal-label">Your card</p>
                    <p class="tap__signal-q">Is it active and usable?</p>
                  </li>

                  <li class="tap__signal" data-s="3">
                    <span class="tap__signal-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <p class="tap__signal-label">This payment</p>
                    <p class="tap__signal-q">Does the amount and transaction make sense?</p>
                  </li>

                  <li class="tap__signal" data-s="4">
                    <span class="tap__signal-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <p class="tap__signal-label">Risk signals</p>
                    <p class="tap__signal-q">Does anything look unusual?</p>
                  </li>
                </ul>

                <p class="tap__reveal-kicker">
                  These signals help the issuer decide whether to approve the payment.
                </p>
                <p class="tap__reveal-text">
                  The exact checks vary by bank, card and transaction.
                </p>

                <!-- The way onward: the decision is made, but it is still
                     sitting where it was made. -->
                <button type="button" class="tap__turn" data-back>
                  Then how did “Approved” get back? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                </button>

                <!-- ====================================================
                     SCENE 6 — the answer comes home.

                     The same four parts as Scene 4, in the opposite order:
                     the bank now sits where "you" stood and you sit where
                     the bank stood. Arrows still point right, so the chain
                     is read the same way it has been all story — what is
                     reversed is the journey, not the reading direction.

                     What crosses is no longer the unlabelled mark Scene 2
                     sent out. It is a labelled result, and it stays where
                     it lands rather than fading, so a reader arriving after
                     the animation still sees "APPROVED came back and the
                     terminal has it" rather than an empty stretch.

                     The terminal's screen only lights once the result has
                     reached it — that ordering is the whole causal point of
                     the beat, and it is why the screen is not lit from the
                     start. -->
                <div class="tap__return">
                  <p class="tap__answered">The answer travelled back.</p>

                  <div class="tap__chain" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span class="tap__step" data-r="1">
                      <span class="tap__step-label tap__step-label--answer">Your bank</span>
                      <span class="tap__step-art">
                        <span class="tap__bank"><span class="tap__bank-mark"></span></span>
                      </span>
                    </span>

                    <span class="tap__link" data-r="2">→</span>

                    <!-- Still unlabelled, as locked in Scene 3. -->
                    <span class="tap__step" data-r="3">
                      <span class="tap__step-art">
                        <span class="tap__route tap__route--return">
                          <span class="tap__route-mark"></span>
                          <span class="tap__route-mark"></span>
                          <span class="tap__route-mark"></span>
                          <span class="tap__approved">Approved</span>
                        </span>
                      </span>
                    </span>

                    <span class="tap__link" data-r="4">→</span>

                    <span class="tap__step" data-r="5">
                      <span class="tap__step-label">Merchant</span>
                      <span class="tap__step-art">
                        <span class="tap__terminal">
                          <span class="tap__terminal-screen tap__terminal-screen--got"></span>
                          <span class="tap__terminal-keys"></span>
                        </span>
                      </span>
                    </span>

                    <span class="tap__link" data-r="6">→</span>

                    <span class="tap__step" data-r="7">
                      <span class="tap__step-label">You</span>
                      <span class="tap__step-art">
                        <span class="tap__phone"><span class="tap__phone-speaker"></span></span>
                      </span>
                    </span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="tap__sr-only">
                    The same chain in the opposite order, with the result travelling
                    from your bank back to the terminal.
                  </p>

                  <p class="tap__reveal-kicker">
                    The issuer sent its decision back through the payment system.
                  </p>
                  <p class="tap__reveal-text">
                    The terminal received the result and showed you Approved.
                  </p>

                  <!-- The way onward. -->
                  <button type="button" class="tap__turn" data-all>
                    All that from one tap? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                  </button>

                  <!-- ====================================================
                       SCENE 7 — the whole thing at once.

                       The story stops drawing boxes here. Every earlier beat
                       used nodes; this one compresses the same journey into
                       type alone, because synthesis should feel lighter than
                       the thing it summarises, not like a sixth diagram.

                       Both legs are cells of ONE grid rather than two
                       separate rows, so the columns line up exactly — "You"
                       sits above "You", the unnamed stretch above the
                       unnamed stretch. That alignment is what lets the
                       reader see it is the same journey twice, once each
                       way, rather than two unrelated lines.

                       The arrows flip direction on the way back while the
                       stops stay in place, so the reversal is legible
                       without the reader having to re-read right-to-left.

                       Scene 8 (the plain-language answer to "who said yes")
                       is not built yet. -->
                  <div class="tap__whole">
                    <p class="tap__conversation">One tap. A whole conversation.</p>

                    <div class="tap__journey" aria-hidden="true">
                      <span class="tap__leg-label" data-j="1">Out</span>
                      <span class="tap__stop" data-j="1">You</span>
                      <span class="tap__dir" data-j="1">→</span>
                      <span class="tap__stop" data-j="1">Merchant</span>
                      <span class="tap__dir" data-j="1">→</span>
                      <span class="tap__stop tap__stop--dots" data-j="1">···</span>
                      <span class="tap__dir" data-j="1">→</span>
                      <span class="tap__stop tap__stop--key" data-j="1">Your bank</span>

                      <span class="tap__leg-label" data-j="2">Back</span>
                      <span class="tap__stop" data-j="2">You</span>
                      <span class="tap__dir" data-j="2">←</span>
                      <span class="tap__stop" data-j="2">Merchant</span>
                      <span class="tap__dir" data-j="2">←</span>
                      <span class="tap__stop tap__stop--dots" data-j="2">···</span>
                      <span class="tap__dir" data-j="2">←</span>
                      <span class="tap__stop tap__stop--key" data-j="2">Approved</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="tap__sr-only">
                      The journey out — you, the merchant, the unnamed systems
                      between, your bank — and the same journey back, carrying the
                      approval.
                    </p>

                    <p class="tap__reveal-kicker">
                      You only saw the beginning and the end.
                    </p>
                    <p class="tap__reveal-text">
                      In between, a request travelled out, a decision was made, and
                      the answer travelled back.
                    </p>

                    <p class="tap__seconds">All in seconds.</p>

                    <!-- The way onward: back to the question the card opened
                         with, to be answered plainly rather than explained
                         again. -->
                    <button type="button" class="tap__turn" data-said>
                      So who said yes? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                    </button>

                    <!-- ====================================================
                         SCENE 8 — the end of Card 4.

                         Closure, not another lesson. Nothing here explains
                         how the request travelled, what was checked, what an
                         issuer is, or how the path is arranged — all of that
                         is behind the reader now, and repeating it would
                         turn the ending into a recap.

                         The three short statements are just that: three
                         statements. No arrows, no nodes, no numbering, no
                         chain — the story has finished drawing things.

                         The whole beat exists so that "You tapped.
                         Approved." — the same four words the card opened on,
                         still sitting unchanged in the left anchor — reads
                         differently the second time. That is why it is set
                         as the largest line here and why nothing follows it
                         except the quiet line acknowledging the change.

                         "Usually" and "the bank behind your card" are both
                         load-bearing and must not be simplified to "your
                         bank decided": the deciding party is the issuer,
                         which is usually but not always a bank. -->
                    <div class="tap__close">
                      <p class="tap__verdict">
                        <span class="tap__verdict-a">Not the terminal.</span>
                        <span class="tap__verdict-b">Usually, the bank behind your card.</span>
                      </p>

                      <div class="tap__resolve">
                        <p class="tap__resolve-line" data-c="1">The terminal asked.</p>
                        <p class="tap__resolve-line" data-c="2">The issuer decided.</p>
                        <p class="tap__resolve-line" data-c="3">The answer came back.</p>
                      </div>

                      <p class="tap__echo">You tapped. Approved.</p>
                      <p class="tap__now">Now you know what happened in between.</p>

                      <!-- The end of the card: the way on is another story,
                           so this is a real link rather than another beat. -->
                      <a class="tap__turn tap__turn--link" href="/explore/">
                        Explore another <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                      </a>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .tap {
    padding-bottom: clamp(60px, 9vh, 110px);
  }

  .tap__stage {
    max-width: 1180px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(32px, 5vh, 48px);
  }

  /* Same threshold every other Explore story splits at. */
  @media (min-width: 980px) {
    .tap__stage {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.86fr) minmax(0, 1.14fr);
      gap: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 68px);
    }
  }

  .tap__copy {
    text-align: left;
  }

  /* ConceptHero's own eyebrow, unchanged: small saffron dot, cobalt
     uppercase sans — the same treatment the other Explore openings already
     reuse. */
  .tap__eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--cobalt);
  }

  .tap__eyebrow span {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--saffron);
  }

  /* Same serif, same size, same weight as every other Explore opening. */
  .tap__opening {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(27px, 3.4vw, 40px);
    line-height: 1.18;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
  }

  .tap__noticed {
    margin: clamp(16px, 2.2vh, 22px) 0 0;
    max-width: 34ch;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .tap__show {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: clamp(20px, 3vh, 30px);
    padding: 12px 22px 12px 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 640;
    cursor: pointer;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 26px rgba(40, 44, 60, 0.1);
    transition: transform 220ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.3, 1), box-shadow 220ms ease,
      opacity 320ms ease, background-color 320ms ease, color 320ms ease;
  }

  .tap__show:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 16px 34px rgba(40, 44, 60, 0.15);
  }

  .tap__show:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--cobalt);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .tap__show span {
    color: var(--saffron);
    transition: transform 220ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .tap__show:hover span {
    transform: translateX(3px);
  }

  /* Used, not gone, once Scene 2 exists — the same softening the other
     stories give their own opening pill applies here. Pre-declared now so
     the button doesn't need touching when that scene is built. */
  [data-stage='2'] .tap__show {
    color: var(--muted);
    background: rgba(255, 253, 250, 0.6);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(40, 44, 60, 0.06);
  }

  [data-stage='2'] .tap__show:hover {
    transform: none;
  }

  .tap__visuals {
    display: block;
  }

  .tap__scene {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 1536 / 1024;
  }

  /* Scene 2 will take the column over entirely — the photo isn't behind it
     or faded under it, it simply stops being shown, the same way every other
     Explore beat's spent frame leaves the flow for the one that replaces
     it. */
  [data-stage='2'] .tap__scene {
    display: none;
  }

  .tap__art {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  /* ====================================================
     SCENE 2 — the tap happened here; the decision didn't
     ==================================================== */

  .tap__moment {
    display: none;
  }

  [data-stage='2'] .tap__moment {
    display: block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 560ms;
  }

  .tap__travelled {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  [data-stage='2'] .tap__moment > .tap__travelled {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 560ms;
  }

  .tap__diagram {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    margin: clamp(30px, 4.6vh, 44px) 0 0;
  }

  /* Everything the reader actually saw, kept together as one thing. */
  .tap__here {
    display: block;
    flex: none;
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .tap__here-label {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .tap__here-art {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .tap__phone {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    flex: none;
    width: 26px;
    height: 44px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(40, 44, 60, 0.24);
    border-radius: 5px;
  }

  .tap__phone-speaker {
    position: absolute;
    top: 5px;
    left: 50%;
    width: 8px;
    height: 2px;
    border-radius: 1px;
    background: rgba(40, 44, 60, 0.22);
    transform: translateX(-50%);
  }

  .tap__to {
    color: var(--muted-light);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  /* A terminal by outline only: a screen and a key area, nothing branded,
     nothing on the screen. */
  .tap__terminal {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 5px;
    flex: none;
    width: 42px;
    height: 52px;
    padding: 5px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(40, 44, 60, 0.24);
    border-radius: 5px;
  }

  .tap__terminal-screen {
    width: 100%;
    height: 20px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: rgba(40, 44, 60, 0.1);
  }

  .tap__terminal-keys {
    width: 100%;
    height: 14px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: rgba(40, 44, 60, 0.05);
  }

  /* The gap is the idea: real empty space where the invisible part of the
     moment happened. */
  .tap__gap {
    position: relative;
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-width: clamp(64px, 11vw, 132px);
    max-width: 190px;
    height: 44px;
    margin: 22px clamp(14px, 2.4vw, 24px) 0;
  }

  /* The request. Unlabelled on purpose, and it never arrives — it fades
     before the question mark, because what it reaches is what this beat
     won't answer yet. */
  .tap__request {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 0;
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    margin-top: -3.5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--cobalt);
    opacity: 0;
  }

  [data-stage='2'] .tap__request {
    animation: tap-travel 2900ms cubic-bezier(0.32, 0, 0.5, 1) 1900ms infinite;
  }

  @keyframes tap-travel {
    0% {
      left: 0;
      opacity: 0;
    }

    10% {
      opacity: 1;
    }

    62% {
      left: calc(100% - 7px);
      opacity: 1;
    }

    76% {
      left: calc(100% - 7px);
      opacity: 0;
    }

    100% {
      left: calc(100% - 7px);
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }

  .tap__unknown {
    flex: none;
    margin-top: 20px;
    color: var(--muted-light);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 46px);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1;
    opacity: 0;
  }

  [data-stage='2'] .tap__here {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1080ms;
  }

  [data-stage='2'] .tap__unknown {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1560ms;
  }

  .tap__sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  /* The same blue kicker / plain supporting-line pair every other Explore
     beat uses for its own explanation. */
  .tap__reveal-kicker {
    display: none;
    margin: clamp(30px, 4.2vh, 40px) 0 0;
    color: var(--cobalt);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  [data-stage='2'] .tap__moment > .tap__reveal-kicker {
    display: block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 2500ms;
  }

  .tap__reveal-text {
    display: none;
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    max-width: 40ch;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  [data-stage='2'] .tap__moment > .tap__reveal-text {
    display: block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 2740ms;
  }

  /* The same quiet page-turn idiom every other Explore story uses. */
  .tap__turn {
    display: none;
    margin: clamp(24px, 3.4vh, 32px) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.006em;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  [data-stage='2'] .tap__moment > .tap__turn {
    display: inline-block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 3220ms;
  }

  .tap__turn span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    margin-left: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--saffron);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 11px;
    vertical-align: middle;
    transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease;
  }

  .tap__turn:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .tap__turn:hover span {
    transform: translateX(2px);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(232, 117, 36, 0.35);
  }

  .tap__turn:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--cobalt);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* ====================================================
     SCENE 3 — the request finds its way
     ==================================================== */

  [data-path='1'] .tap__moment > .tap__travelled,
  [data-path='1'] .tap__moment > .tap__diagram,
  [data-path='1'] .tap__moment > .tap__sr-only,
  [data-path='1'] .tap__moment > .tap__reveal-kicker,
  [data-path='1'] .tap__moment > .tap__reveal-text,
  [data-path='1'] .tap__moment > .tap__turn {
    display: none;
  }

  .tap__path {
    display: none;
  }

  [data-path='1'] .tap__moment > .tap__path {
    display: block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 240ms;
  }

  .tap__found {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  [data-path='1'] .tap__path > .tap__found {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 240ms;
  }

  /* One horizontal run, wrapping on narrow screens rather than scrolling. */
  .tap__chain {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: clamp(10px, 1.8vw, 18px);
    margin: clamp(30px, 4.6vh, 44px) 0 0;
  }

  .tap__step {
    display: block;
    flex: none;
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .tap__step-label {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .tap__step-art {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .tap__link {
    flex: none;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    color: var(--muted-light);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1;
    opacity: 0;
  }

  /* The payment path: one neutral stretch holding a few unnamed marks.
     Nothing inside is labelled or distinguishable — naming any of it is
     precisely what this beat is not ready to do. */
  .tap__route {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-around;
    flex: none;
    width: clamp(84px, 12vw, 116px);
    height: 52px;
    padding: 0 10px;
    border: 1px dashed rgba(40, 44, 60, 0.26);
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .tap__route-mark {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: rgba(40, 44, 60, 0.2);
  }

  /* The same question mark Scene 2 ended on, simply further along. */
  .tap__unknown--chain {
    margin-top: 0;
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .tap__step--end .tap__step-art {
    height: 52px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  [data-path='1'] .tap__step[data-step='1'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 820ms;
  }

  [data-path='1'] .tap__link[data-step='2'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1120ms;
  }

  [data-path='1'] .tap__step[data-step='3'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1420ms;
  }

  [data-path='1'] .tap__link[data-step='4'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1760ms;
  }

  [data-path='1'] .tap__step[data-step='5'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 2020ms;
  }

  [data-path='1'] .tap__path > .tap__reveal-kicker {
    display: block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 2680ms;
  }

  [data-path='1'] .tap__path > .tap__reveal-text {
    display: block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 2920ms;
  }

  [data-path='1'] .tap__path > .tap__turn {
    display: inline-block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 3400ms;
  }

  /* ====================================================
     SCENE 4 — the question mark resolves
     ==================================================== */

  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__path > .tap__found,
  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__path > .tap__chain,
  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__path > .tap__sr-only,
  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__path > .tap__reveal-kicker,
  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__path > .tap__reveal-text,
  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__path > .tap__turn {
    display: none;
  }

  .tap__issuer {
    display: none;
  }

  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__path > .tap__issuer {
    display: block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 240ms;
  }

  .tap__usually {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__issuer > .tap__usually {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 240ms;
  }

  /* The answer, standing exactly where the question mark stood. Solid and
     cobalt against the dashed grey of the stretch before it, so the eye
     lands on it as the one named thing at the end of the chain. */
  .tap__bank {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex: none;
    width: 52px;
    height: 52px;
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(36, 92, 255, 0.55);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: rgba(36, 92, 255, 0.06);
  }

  .tap__bank-mark {
    width: 16px;
    height: 4px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--cobalt);
  }

  .tap__step-label--answer {
    color: var(--cobalt);
  }

  /* Holds the two sentences on their own lines, so the break falls where
     the sense does rather than wherever the measure happens to run out.
     Type, colour and spacing are inherited unchanged. */
  .tap__line {
    display: block;
  }

  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__step[data-i='1'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 820ms;
  }

  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__link[data-i='2'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1040ms;
  }

  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__step[data-i='3'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1260ms;
  }

  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__link[data-i='4'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1480ms;
  }

  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__step[data-i='5'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1700ms;
  }

  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__link[data-i='6'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1960ms;
  }

  /* The reveal itself, given a beat of its own before it lands. */
  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__step[data-i='7'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 2280ms;
  }

  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__issuer > .tap__reveal-kicker {
    display: block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 2960ms;
  }

  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__issuer > .tap__reveal-text {
    display: block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 3200ms;
  }

  [data-issuer='1'] .tap__issuer > .tap__turn {
    display: inline-block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 3680ms;
  }

  /* ====================================================
     SCENE 5 — more than one thing
     ==================================================== */

  [data-signals='1'] .tap__issuer > .tap__usually,
  [data-signals='1'] .tap__issuer > .tap__chain,
  [data-signals='1'] .tap__issuer > .tap__sr-only,
  [data-signals='1'] .tap__issuer > .tap__reveal-kicker,
  [data-signals='1'] .tap__issuer > .tap__reveal-text,
  [data-signals='1'] .tap__issuer > .tap__turn {
    display: none;
  }

  .tap__signals {
    display: none;
  }

  [data-signals='1'] .tap__issuer > .tap__signals {
    display: block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 240ms;
  }

  .tap__notone {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  [data-signals='1'] .tap__signals > .tap__notone {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 240ms;
  }

  /* A grid, not a row: two by two reads as a set considered together,
     where a single line with arrows would read as stages. */
  .tap__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: clamp(22px, 3.4vh, 30px) clamp(24px, 4vw, 44px);
    margin: clamp(28px, 4.4vh, 40px) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 620px) {
    .tap__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .tap__signal {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 18px;
    opacity: 0;
  }

  /* One small mark per signal, identical on all four — a quiet anchor for
     the eye, never a bullet that implies a list order or a status light
     that implies a result. */
  .tap__signal-mark {
    position: absolute;
    top: 5px;
    left: 0;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--cobalt);
  }

  .tap__signal-label {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .tap__signal-q {
    margin: 7px 0 0;
    max-width: 30ch;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(16px, 1.8vw, 19px);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.32;
    letter-spacing: -0.014em;
  }

  /* Tight enough that the four settle as one group rather than counting
     themselves out in sequence. */
  [data-signals='1'] .tap__signal[data-s='1'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 820ms;
  }

  [data-signals='1'] .tap__signal[data-s='2'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 940ms;
  }

  [data-signals='1'] .tap__signal[data-s='3'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1060ms;
  }

  [data-signals='1'] .tap__signal[data-s='4'] {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1180ms;
  }

  [data-signals='1'] .tap__signals > .tap__reveal-kicker {
    display: block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1900ms;
  }

  [data-signals='1'] .tap__signals > .tap__reveal-text {
    display: block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 2140ms;
  }

  [data-signals='1'] .tap__signals > .tap__turn {
    display: inline-block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 2620ms;
  }

  /* ====================================================
     SCENE 6 — the answer comes home
     ==================================================== */

  [data-return='1'] .tap__signals > .tap__notone,
  [data-return='1'] .tap__signals > .tap__grid,
  [data-return='1'] .tap__signals > .tap__reveal-kicker,
  [data-return='1'] .tap__signals > .tap__reveal-text,
  [data-return='1'] .tap__signals > .tap__turn {
    display: none;
  }

  .tap__return {
    display: none;
  }

  [data-return='1'] .tap__signals > .tap__return {
    display: block;
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 240ms;
  }

  .tap__answered {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  [data-return='1'] .tap__return > .tap__answered {
    animation: tap-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 240ms;
  }

  /* Wider than the outbound stretch, purely so the labelled result has
     room to visibly cross it. --chip is the payload's own width, used by
     the keyframe so the travel always stops flush at the far edge. */
  .tap__route--return {
    position: relative;
    --chip: 78px;
    width: clamp(124px, 19vw, 210px);
  }

  @media (max-width: 619px) {
    .tap__route--return {
      --chip: 70px;
    }
  }

  .tap__route--return .tap__route-mark {
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  /* The payload, labelled this time. It stays where it lands rather than
